Shader input submission:
  Source: Conversation revision: ordinary assignments retain inputs; Use() invokes contract-generated Submit().
  Goal: Publish the complete retained state once before drawing or dispatching, with no setter GPU effects.
  Scope: Graphics and compute owners, resource contracts, shared inputs and application/engine callers.
  Excludes: Prepare callbacks, same-frame allocation caching, cross-frame reuse and new benchmarks.

  ✔ Establish the lifecycle contract and inventory consumers.
    - Contract: Rendering.ShaderPreparation.md; migration sites: Rendering.ShaderPreparation.Inventory.md.
    - Use is the publication boundary. Assignments persist without an editing scope or runtime rollback.
    - Existing binding interfaces declare runtime sources as retained properties or authored resource getters.
    - The generator emits Submit from those contracts; static/offline declarations remain metadata.
    - Preserve explicit ConfigureOptions transactions and existing executable lifecycle rules.

  ✔ Implement the shared lifecycle and generated reference consumers.
    - Remove Prepare generation, editing scopes and preparation-failure poisoning.
    - Generate staged resource setters and Submit; reject bindings without a runtime source.
    - Reuse existing CPU packing, block identities and layout resolution; support CPU block source getters.
    - Stage upsample and probe anchor assignments before Use in their renderer callers.
    - Retain repeated Use, engine/interface routing, failure cleanup, reload and actual resource restoration.
    - Completion: Subagent-run CPU/GPU and generator tests plus independent review confirm the revised design.
    - Validation: Debug build, 97/97 distinct focused CPU/GPU tests and 140/140 generator tests passed; no skips.
      Evidence: ../artifacts/submission-tests/submission-final.trx, ring-final.trx and generator-final.trx.
      Second source review and independent audit passed. Headless checks only; no game launched.

  ✔ Migrate all shaders and callers to the contract.
    - Convert authored resource setters to retained/generated properties and CPU blocks to source getters.
    - Remove temporary authored compatibility Submit overrides once their owners and callers are migrated.
    - Replace the temporary shared-lighting opt-in with contract source getters throughout shared bases.
    - Convert graphics and compute callers to assign inputs before use and draw/dispatch.
    - Give engine-driven liquid adapters a verified pre-draw boundary before removing setter publication.
    - Preserve barriers, explicit clears, readbacks, upload ownership and current-generation layout resolution.
    - Remove obsolete immediate-submit helpers and unused UBO batch scopes.
    - Completion: Reconcile the inventory; any remaining immediate binding is an explicit low-level operation or adapter.
    - Validation: 398 shader variants rebuilt; focused CPU/GPU run passed 856 tests with 4 existing skips;
      generator run passed 150/150. Fresh world-history/surface-lighting regression run passed 60/60.
      Evidence: ../VanillaGraphicsExpanded.Tests/TestResults/migration-final-focused.trx,
      ../VanillaGraphicsExpanded.Tests/TestResults/migration-metadata-runtime.trx,
      and ../ShaderContractGenerator.Tests/TestResults/migration-generator-final.trx.
    - Final atmosphere/scope recheck: 28/28 passed, including enclosing compute SSBO restoration;
      ../VanillaGraphicsExpanded.Tests/TestResults/migration-atmosphere-final.trx. Latest Debug build passed.
      Second source review and independent test/inventory review found no remaining migration gaps.

  ☐ Validate and document the completed contract.
    - Test retained/default values, partial assignments, generated binding coverage, submission failure/retry,
      nested scopes/restoration, reload, required/optional resources, frame rollover and both ring paths.
    - Verify several assignments followed by Use publish one active CPU block; do not claim frame-time savings.
    - Update authoring guidance and resource lifetime responsibilities.
    - Perform second review and independent audit before completion; no game launch for acceptance.
    - Broader-suite follow-up: assess trace sun and debug/registration-count expectations, accessor reload queues,
      PBR mode lifecycle, installed-engine GLSL/depth fixtures, terrain GLSL variables and the raw SPIR-V GL error.
      The broad run was interrupted; these exclusions are not established baseline failures or a clean-suite result.
